(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "260726-content-protection-mvp")
  (:adr/title "ai-gftd-content-protection — rights-safe monitoring and human-approved platform reporting")
  (:adr/status "active")
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/topic "content-protection")
  (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-26")
  (:adr/body "# Decision\n\nCreate `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-content-protection` as the product boundary for monitoring unauthorized TikTok/YouTube reposts and clips. Reuse the vocabulary of deepfakeTakedown and the relisting lifecycle of kakure, but do not overload either product: deepfakeTakedown is synthetic-media incident data; kakure is personal-data erasure.\n\nThe MVP separates detection from legal assertion. Platform adapters ingest candidates, fingerprint workers produce independent video/audio/transcript evidence, pure CLJC scores candidates, and an accountable human must approve before a report package can be finalized. Automatic platform submission is explicitly disabled. A package fails closed without rights provenance, a content snapshot, minimum match/overlap, verified contact, and good-faith/accuracy declarations.\n\n# Database\n\nThe durable source of truth is the Cloudflare-accessed, PostgreSQL-backed Kotobase database. The application uses the current `kotobase.core` Datomic-shaped API (`open`, `transact!`, `datoms`, `q`, `query`, `pull`), with `kotobase-storage-postgres` below the provider-neutral storage boundary. It does not build new code on the legacy document/stream `IStore`. PostgreSQL credentials, datasource/Hyperdrive construction, encryption/blind-index controls and CACAO authorization stay in the host; the app receives an open database. Memory stores are test oracles only and production fails closed without host injection.\n\n# Boundaries\n\nThe product does not decide fair use as a legal conclusion, scrape around platform access controls, report identity/style similarity, or suppress criticism. YouTube/TikTok API and official-form transports remain adapters because platform eligibility, credentials, and fields change independently of the evidence core.\n\n# Implemented\n\nReference validation, deterministic evidence scoring, human review, report readiness, audit package generation, enforcement lifecycle, relisting detection, Kotobase Datomic persistence, schema, CLI doctor, and tests are implemented in the standalone project. External discovery, media fingerprint extraction, authenticated UI, and official submission adapters are follow-up integration work.")))
